rl":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T19:35:25Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T19:35:25Z","body":"> Will tracking a dynamic target cause it to be lost or out of sync? In this PR.\r\n\r\nWhat this PR changed is how the navmesh graph is build and synchronized. Your target tracking happens outside the navigation system and as such is unaffected.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560208344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695492000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100497#issuecomment-2695492000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100497","id":2695492000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gqfGg","user":{"login":"InfiniteCactusDev","id":145286353,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKjk0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145286353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev","html_url":"https://github.com/InfiniteCactusDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfiniteCactusDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-03T20:42:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T08:47:33Z","body":"Thanks for another awesome addition to the navigation functionally @smix8!\r\n\r\nOne question:\r\n\r\nWith the old/sync version of the navigation logic the way I used to know if the navigation was updated and synced I used the BakeFinished signal from NavigationRegion2D and then await a ProcessFrame signal (in c# so some naming might be slightly off).\r\n\r\nThis now obviously no longer works since the sync might take longer than a frame.\r\nIs there an alternative method to know if the navigation is done syncing?\r\n\r\nEdit: Looks like `NavigationServer2D.MapChanged` can be used now","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695492000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]